    {
      "id": "689091aa29aa-q4",
      "number": 4,
      "question": "Which of the following is NOT a component of a flower? &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2347;&#2370;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366; &#2328;&#2335;&#2325; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following is NOT a component of a flower?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2347;&#2370;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366; &#2328;&#2335;&#2325; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;?</span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Androecium &#2346;&#2369;&#2350;&#2306;&#2327;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Androecium</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2346;&#2369;&#2350;&#2306;&#2327;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Corolla &#2325;&#2379;&#2352;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Corolla</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2379;&#2352;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Spines &#2325;&#2366;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Spines</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2366;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Calyx &#2325;&#2381;&#2354;&#2376;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Calyx</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2381;&#2354;&#2376;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p>A flower consists of four main parts - Calyx (sepals), Corolla (petals), Androecium (male reproductive part), and Gynoecium (female reproductive part). Spines are modified leaves or stem structures found in some plants for defense but are not a floral component.</p>",
