      "number": 10,
      "question": "Which of the following statements best defines monoecious? Options: &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2325;&#2341;&#2344; &#2319;&#2325;&#2354;&#2367;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2360;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2379;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;? &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346;:",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following statements best defines monoecious?</p><p><b>Options:</b></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2325;&#2341;&#2344; &#2319;&#2325;&#2354;&#2367;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2360;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2379;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2359;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p><b>&#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346;:</b></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "A flower with both androecium and gynoecium &#2319;&#2325; &#2347;&#2370;&#2354; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2369;&#2306;&#2325;&#2375;&#2360;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; &#2332;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366;&#2306;&#2327; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">A flower with both androecium and gynoecium</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;&#2325; &#2347;&#2370;&#2354; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2369;&#2306;&#2325;&#2375;&#2360;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; &#2332;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366;&#2306;&#2327; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "A flower with dithecous anther &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340; &#2346;&#2352;&#2366;&#2327;&#2325;&#2379;&#2358; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2347;&#2370;&#2354;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">A flower with dithecous anther</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340; &#2346;&#2352;&#2366;&#2327;&#2325;&#2379;&#2358; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2347;&#2370;&#2354;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "A flower with gynoecium only &#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; &#2332;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366;&#2306;&#2327; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2347;&#2370;&#2354;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">A flower with gynoecium only</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; &#2332;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366;&#2306;&#2327; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2347;&#2370;&#2354;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "A flower with androecium only &#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; &#2319;&#2306;&#2337;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2360;&#2368;&#2351;&#2350; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2347;&#2370;&#2354;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">A flower with androecium only</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; &#2319;&#2306;&#2337;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2360;&#2368;&#2351;&#2350; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2347;&#2370;&#2354;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<p>1 <b>Definition of Monoecious:</b></p><p>o A monoecious plant or flower has both male reproductive structures (<b>androecium</b>) and female reproductive structures (<b>gynoecium</b>) within the same individual plant.</p><p>o This allows the plant to self-pollinate or cross-pollinate.</p><p>2) <b>Examples:</b></p><p>o Plants like maize and cucurbits (e.g., pumpkins, squash) are monoecious.</p><p>3) <b>Incorrect Options:</b></p><p>o <b>Option 2 (Dithecous anther):</b> Refers to an anther with two lobes, unrelated to monoecy.</p><p>o <b>Option 3 (Gynoecium only):</b> Refers to a unisexual female flower.</p><p>o <b>Option 4 (Androecium only):</b> Refers to a unisexual male flower.</p>",
